==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etym|gmh|de}} {{term|roum|lang=gmh}}. The expected modern form would be ''Raum'', which has been ousted by a dialectal form due to the identicalness with {{term|Raum||room|lang=de}} (from Middle High German {{term|rūm|lang=gmh}}). Dialects that have developed Middle High German ''-ou-'' into ''-ā-'' are found in south-eastern and central-western Germany. Cognate with Dutch {{term|room|lang=nl}}.

